# L §5.10 Parts (2.1-F10): "the sign rule is not checked against a hole balance, as in 2.0" (E §4.2 step 5), the arrival
# side of the migrator's F-h: acc, owned and min 0, opens at 0; inc brings the hole amount got (ania_tomek's by the
# community rule), then out takes a fixed 50.00.  The balance after inc is a hole; inc's part is one hole part of the
# hole balance, possibly ania_tomek's only, and out's take reaches it: no RUN-PLACE.  q1: the balance's hole (got),
# read of parts included.  q2: out took 50.00 (a_out carried through) from parts whose every possible label is
# ania_tomek's (L §8.1, 2.1-F12).  Before: `out takes acc below 0` (the hole arrival added no part).
=== m.tally
model t10
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "test"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

kind couples: parties

kind persons: parties

kind cash_accounts: place one min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(DUK)
  takes k for w order rank[k.owner]

place acc: cash_accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2000-01-01..

input got: money DUK question "how much came in?"

input d_in: date

input d_out: date

input a_out: money DUK

def rank[p in parties]: int = ?"which money leaves first?" at reader

def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = (if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0)

move inc: transfers
  on d_in
  at d_in
  leg cash from world to acc amount got

move out: transfers
  on d_out
  at d_out
  leg cash from acc to world amount a_out

ask q1: bal(acc, 2025-04-30), bal(acc, 2025-04-30) of ania_tomek

ask q2: out.cash.amount of ania_tomek

version cast
  cite src
  known 2021-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1991-03-14..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1989-07-02..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2016-09-10..

version facts
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2021-01-01
  opening[acc] = 0 at 2025-01-01 start
  d_in = 2025-02-01
  d_out = 2025-03-01
  a_out = 50.00
=== expect
q1: (?"how much came in?" (got), ?"how much came in?" (got))
...
q2: 50.00 DUK
...
